(6627577, 989462, 69572, '<td valign="top">I only ever give one 10 when voting.  This was just such a peaceful well lit shot.  Hope you win</td>', 'I only ever give one 10 when voting.  This was just such a peaceful well lit shot.  Hope you win', '2011-12-29 04:33:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627608, 988868, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>Interesting interpretation of the theme.<br/>I love the orangey-yellow and blue combination  you used. It works well together. the lightbulb and the cord are very clever with the bright light source behind (?) the bulb really pulling your title together and optically standing out and drawing my eye. <br/>I don''t understand the big light reflection in the bottom half of the picture though. IMO it detracts from the bulb and light at the top. I feel the whole bottom could have been cropped out. In the present pic you could have also edited the little yellow "smudge" out at the bottom of the Photo just making the image tidier.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!Interesting interpretation of the theme.I love the orangey-yellow and blue combination  you used. It works well together. the lightbulb and the cord are very clever with the bright light source behind (?) the bulb really pulling your title together and optically standing out and drawing my eye. I don''t understand the big light reflection in the bottom half of the picture though. IMO it detracts from the bulb and light at the top. I feel the whole bottom could have been cropped out. In the present pic you could have also edited the little yellow "smudge" out at the bottom of the Photo just making the image tidier.', '2011-12-29 07:20:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627609, 989465, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>OK, this is gross - but I suppose such a reaction to a photograph is a good thing ;-). I think your interpretation of the theme is somewhat outside the "usual", but definitely within the theme. I like the way you dealt with the background (or lack thereof) which really brings the face and hand to the forfront. I am not sure if the skin tone is not a bit on the "red" side. What I don''t like so much is the prominence of the hand in this photo. Your title was "finger" + nose, yet the hand is the largest item in the picture. Perhaps shooting with a different lense, or cropping it tighter would have put more emphasise on the finger. I do love the models nose for this theme. and based on the whole take on the title, I like the "goofiness" that the model portraits.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!OK, this is gross - but I suppose such a reaction to a photograph is a good thing ;-). I think your interpretation of the theme is somewhat outside the "usual", but definitely within the theme. I like the way you dealt with the background (or lack thereof) which really brings the face and hand to the forfront. I am not sure if the skin tone is not a bit on the "red" side. What I don''t like so much is the prominence of the hand in this photo. Your title was "finger" + nose, yet the hand is the largest item in the picture. Perhaps shooting with a different lense, or cropping it tighter would have put more emphasise on the finger. I do love the models nose for this theme. and based on the whole take on the title, I like the "goofiness" that the model portraits.', '2011-12-29 07:20:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627610, 989411, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I think the interpretation of the theme is good. I like that you used dolls rather than real people and still could get the "husband&amp;wife" theme across. My eyes are drawn a lot to the background though. Especially the little boys pictures on the wall. the blue in those pics is very strong and draws my eye. Perhaps a brighter attire of the H&amp;W or a shallower DOF would have emphasised the main charaters more. I do like the way you used the lighting.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I think the interpretation of the theme is good. I like that you used dolls rather than real people and still could get the "husband&wife" theme across. My eyes are drawn a lot to the background though. Especially the little boys pictures on the wall. the blue in those pics is very strong and draws my eye. Perhaps a brighter attire of the H&W or a shallower DOF would have emphasised the main charaters more. I do like the way you used the lighting.', '2011-12-29 07:20:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627611, 989270, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I think this is an interesting interpretation of the theme. I like the composition of your picture, especially the stick on the diagonal in the light shade. However, not being a drummer or music person myself, I don''t know what the rippley background is and I find my attention being drawn to that "mistery" in your picture almost more than the obvious hands and sticks and thus find it distracting. I do like the tight crop you used it really emphasised not only the hands and sticks but in fact "how" they go together.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I think this is an interesting interpretation of the theme. I like the composition of your picture, especially the stick on the diagonal in the light shade. However, not being a drummer or music person myself, I don''t know what the rippley background is and I find my attention being drawn to that "mistery" in your picture almost more than the obvious hands and sticks and thus find it distracting. I do like the tight crop you used it really emphasised not only the hands and sticks but in fact "how" they go together.', '2011-12-29 07:20:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627614, 989467, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I don''t quite understand how "dice" go with the theme of "A+B". Dice are used singly, in 2s or several, depending on the game they are used for. <br/>In any case, I think the picture is very striking. IMO, I think this is really well put together with the reflective surface at the bottom. Love the crop and placement of the main object. Nothing to distract the eye. Your choice of shutter speed, IMO was also really good. This is one of my favorite photos so far, except that I don''t think it is within the theme, or at least I don''t "get it" :-(.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I don''t quite understand how "dice" go with the theme of "A+B". Dice are used singly, in 2s or several, depending on the game they are used for. In any case, I think the picture is very striking. IMO, I think this is really well put together with the reflective surface at the bottom. Love the crop and placement of the main object. Nothing to distract the eye. Your choice of shutter speed, IMO was also really good. This is one of my favorite photos so far, except that I don''t think it is within the theme, or at least I don''t "get it" :-(.', '2011-12-29 07:27:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627623, 989319, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>You are obviously NOT my brother - he thinks NOTHING goes with raisins ;-). Different take on the theme, I like it. <br/>the raisins came out well in the picture I think and the placement of them is good (grouped together in one spot rather than all over). I do feel the picture is "flat" though and the "flakes" don''t really stand out. This could be the top of a pie crust as well. I don''t know if different lighting and/or higher contrast in post editing would have solved this. <br/>Although it is well within the theme, I am not "captivated" by this photograph.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!You are obviously NOT my brother - he thinks NOTHING goes with raisins ;-). Different take on the theme, I like it. the raisins came out well in the picture I think and the placement of them is good (grouped together in one spot rather than all over). I do feel the picture is "flat" though and the "flakes" don''t really stand out. This could be the top of a pie crust as well. I don''t know if different lighting and/or higher contrast in post editing would have solved this. Although it is well within the theme, I am not "captivated" by this photograph.', '2011-12-29 07:42:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627625, 989394, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>OK, this is well over my head in terms of post editing :-). I keep going back to look at why you did certain things the way you did them regarding the theme of the challange and I personally like that - being challenegd and not everything being "obvious". I love the sky and the bed - the colours, the idea of "heavenly breakfast in bed" (at elast that is my interpretation of your photograph;-)). Other than "balancing" the image, I am not sure why you needed 2 identical but mirror image ladies having breakfast. I would have perhaps also prefered them to be a little more crisp (focus). I DO loke the reflection of the colour of the bed spread on the jacket though, I think that is very clever. I think this is perhaps not the most "beautiful" photo, it lacks some type of "oh" factor for me, but it IS a very clever photo, with, I am sure a lot of work behind it.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!OK, this is well over my head in terms of post editing :-). I keep going back to look at why you did certain things the way you did them regarding the theme of the challange and I personally like that - being challenegd and not everything being "obvious". I love the sky and the bed - the colours, the idea of "heavenly breakfast in bed" (at elast that is my interpretation of your photograph;-)). Other than "balancing" the image, I am not sure why you needed 2 identical but mirror image ladies having breakfast. I would have perhaps also prefered them to be a little more crisp (focus). I DO loke the reflection of the colour of the bed spread on the jacket though, I think that is very clever. I think this is perhaps not the most "beautiful" photo, it lacks some type of "oh" factor for me, but it IS a very clever photo, with, I am sure a lot of work behind it.', '2011-12-29 07:52:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627627, 989038, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I like your interpretation of the theme. I LOVE the bottom part of your photograph - the leaf and the rusty surface. IMO, all you needed was to add a little blue of the background and you could have left it. I find the additional rusty barb wire, which is out of focus and "oversized" compared to the leaf distracting. the oversize, IMO really draws attention to the barb wire and I don''t think that is where the viewers attention should be going. The same for the light reflections. Especially the bright one in the middle catches the eye. I like the colour combination you used and the DOF on the leaf and rusty sheet as well as the lighting on the leaf, making  the shadow go "under" the leaf and hence not obscuring any of the rust it is lying on - very nicely done.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I like your interpretation of the theme. I LOVE the bottom part of your photograph - the leaf and the rusty surface. IMO, all you needed was to add a little blue of the background and you could have left it. I find the additional rusty barb wire, which is out of focus and "oversized" compared to the leaf distracting. the oversize, IMO really draws attention to the barb wire and I don''t think that is where the viewers attention should be going. The same for the light reflections. Especially the bright one in the middle catches the eye. I like the colour combination you used and the DOF on the leaf and rusty sheet as well as the lighting on the leaf, making  the shadow go "under" the leaf and hence not obscuring any of the rust it is lying on - very nicely done.', '2011-12-29 08:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627633, 989132, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I must admit, I had to read up what a waterman is/does - thanks for some education :-). So, I like your interpretation of the theme. I like the way you use the slightly out of focus boat tarpaulin as your backdrop. By the same token, I would have prefered to have the glove, as one of the main items in this image, to be completely in focus and/or more prominent in color and/or placement. I like the mud pattern on the boots, as it prevents them from being a "big black blotch" as well as adding interest and a little more "background" to your theme. I think your lighting is good and the wet surface all over again emphasis the picture''s story.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I must admit, I had to read up what a waterman is/does - thanks for some education :-). So, I like your interpretation of the theme. I like the way you use the slightly out of focus boat tarpaulin as your backdrop. By the same token, I would have prefered to have the glove, as one of the main items in this image, to be completely in focus and/or more prominent in color and/or placement. I like the mud pattern on the boots, as it prevents them from being a "big black blotch" as well as adding interest and a little more "background" to your theme. I think your lighting is good and the wet surface all over again emphasis the picture''s story.', '2011-12-29 08:12:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627637, 989367, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>Clever interpretation of the theme :-). I like your composition with 2 of the same, but one in and one out of focus and the main bacon on the photo''s diagonal. <br/>Your color balance is not right for me. The egg white is yellow, it should be, well, white. The bacon too shows little contrast and I think there is too much reflection on the bacon ? It has somehow lost its 3D aspect, which is a shame. I know food photography is very hard - the professionals use paint and laquer to make the food look the way it does on pics!</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!Clever interpretation of the theme :-). I like your composition with 2 of the same, but one in and one out of focus and the main bacon on the photo''s diagonal. Your color balance is not right for me. The egg white is yellow, it should be, well, white. The bacon too shows little contrast and I think there is too much reflection on the bacon ? It has somehow lost its 3D aspect, which is a shame. I know food photography is very hard - the professionals use paint and laquer to make the food look the way it does on pics!', '2011-12-29 08:19:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627639, 989423, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I like your theme interpretation and I very much like your composition - looks really like a Christmas Card. Personally I have a problem with your choice of focus. It seems the tree is in perfect focus, but the little table with the note, milk etc is just out of focus. Considering the milk etc. is your main theme, I would have done this the other way round, or have everything in focus, which IMO in this image would have worked well, because the tree is fairly dark and your forground would draw the eye anyway. I like the way you made the note and red tablecloth almost look surreal, but I feel you overdid the brightness/highlight of the milk glass, loosing definition on the top of teh glass.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I like your theme interpretation and I very much like your composition - looks really like a Christmas Card. Personally I have a problem with your choice of focus. It seems the tree is in perfect focus, but the little table with the note, milk etc is just out of focus. Considering the milk etc. is your main theme, I would have done this the other way round, or have everything in focus, which IMO in this image would have worked well, because the tree is fairly dark and your forground would draw the eye anyway. I like the way you made the note and red tablecloth almost look surreal, but I feel you overdid the brightness/highlight of the milk glass, loosing definition on the top of teh glass.', '2011-12-29 08:27:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627650, 989466, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I like the way you used the "V" in the sky to frame/draw attention to the 2 people''s faces. I love the colour composition with the sky and the human skin. <br/>I would have cropped the picture a little more to get rid of the girl''s stomach - not because I have an issue with short tops, but because the stomach as well as the man''s arm keep drawing the eye away from the faces (at least it does for me :-)). mabe you could have edited the few reflecting spots out of the background to tidy up the image and also darkened the car on the left a bit more. I think the lighting on the people is good and the soft focus flatters their youthful faces.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I like the way you used the "V" in the sky to frame/draw attention to the 2 people''s faces. I love the colour composition with the sky and the human skin. I would have cropped the picture a little more to get rid of the girl''s stomach - not because I have an issue with short tops, but because the stomach as well as the man''s arm keep drawing the eye away from the faces (at least it does for me :-)). mabe you could have edited the few reflecting spots out of the background to tidy up the image and also darkened the car on the left a bit more. I think the lighting on the people is good and the soft focus flatters their youthful faces.', '2011-12-29 08:39:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627651, 989459, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/> <br/>I have no idea how you took the picture or what you did to it to make it look the way it does, but I love it :-). <br/>Perhaps if the left and right edges could be a bit darker (like the right front corner), putting more focus on the centre and giving a little more contrast. and I am not sure if you could just level it a little? It seems to be tilting to the left, but that may be a trick of the eye due to the coloring as well.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours! I have no idea how you took the picture or what you did to it to make it look the way it does, but I love it :-). Perhaps if the left and right edges could be a bit darker (like the right front corner), putting more focus on the centre and giving a little more contrast. and I am not sure if you could just level it a little? It seems to be tilting to the left, but that may be a trick of the eye due to the coloring as well.', '2011-12-29 08:44:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627653, 989413, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>I like your choice of subject, I don''t understand why you used that title for the image in this challenge. I would have thought "black &amp; white" ... or is that too obvious? :-). <br/>I like the backdrop but I am not convinced of the surface the 2 knights stand on and how it blends into the backdrop. I feel the lighting on the white king is good, but I don''t think it''s right on the black king. I do like the placemnet of your subject for this image.</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!I like your choice of subject, I don''t understand why you used that title for the image in this challenge. I would have thought "black & white" ... or is that too obvious? :-). I like the backdrop but I am not convinced of the surface the 2 knights stand on and how it blends into the backdrop. I feel the lighting on the white king is good, but I don''t think it''s right on the black king. I do like the placemnet of your subject for this image.', '2011-12-29 08:50:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627662, 989289, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>Nice interpretation of the theme. I feel the whole picture is a little lopsided. I want to grab the glass to stop it from sliding off the table :-). Since the main subject of the photo are the cookies AND the milk, perhaps the focus should have been on both, or maybe have the milk prominently as the backdrop without having the black chair there as well. Maybe a different colour table top would have made this composition more intersting and the green decor on the plate is unnecessary as it doesn''t add anything to the picture</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!Nice interpretation of the theme. I feel the whole picture is a little lopsided. I want to grab the glass to stop it from sliding off the table :-). Since the main subject of the photo are the cookies AND the milk, perhaps the focus should have been on both, or maybe have the milk prominently as the backdrop without having the black chair there as well. Maybe a different colour table top would have made this composition more intersting and the green decor on the plate is unnecessary as it doesn''t add anything to the picture', '2011-12-29 09:12:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6627665, 989306, 141319, '<td valign="top">I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!<br/>a nice take on the theme. What a great photograph - when i grow up I want to take pictures like this :-). I like the colour combination - both subjects (branch and bird) really stand out from te background. Nice composition. Only negative I can find is that the left side of the branch is slightly out of focus</td>', 'I apologise, I am new to this and you are "stuck" with my comments. Pls. realise that this is *my* learning curve more than yours!a nice take on the theme. What a great photograph - when i grow up I want to take pictures like this :-). I like the colour combination - both subjects (branch and bird) really stand out from te background. Nice composition. Only negative I can find is that the left side of the branch is slightly out of focus', '2011-12-29 09:16:53.000000', NULL, 1),
